3:["$","figcaption",null,{"children":["Jiansheng, a small farming village on the Sanjiang Plain in eastern Heilongjiang, seen from a plane in August 2016."," ",["$","span",null,{"className":"credit","children":["Photo: ","Ting Chen",","," ",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0/","rel":"license","children":"CC BY-SA 2.0"}],", via"," ",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%BB%BA%E8%83%9C%E6%9D%91_August_2016_in_China.jpg","children":"Wikimedia Commons"}],"."]}]]}]
4:["$","h2","7",{"data-count":"","children":"Do machines replace people?"}]
5:["$","p","8",{"data-count":"","children":["I suggested in the progress check-in that people leave first and machines follow, however a more nuanced story is supported by the major articles and data I’ve seen. The large gently sloping farms are very optimal for machine use, but Northeast Plain farmers ranked a lack of machinery training as the biggest barrier, industrial machines for corn farming cost from US$1,500 to US$15,000 which exposes machinery as an unwise business practice given that farmers earn under US$181.49 per hectare ",["$","span","1",{"className":"cite","children":["(",[["$","span","huo",{"children":["",["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/references/#huo","children":"Huo et al. 2022"}]]}]],")"]}],". Many hire machine services instead despite the higher cost long term."]}]
6:["$","p","9",{"data-count":"","children":["Only 54 percent of Lishu farmers had adopted conservation tillage, and some of the others were ‘informed non-adopters’ who understood the cultivation method but had more faith in traditional practices. I think that the ageing, hesitant workforce is the pressure being handled least well."]}]
